# ─── Frontend (Vite, build-time) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Origin of the standalone HeyQ API in PRODUCTION only. Leave UNSET for local
# development so the vite dev proxy serves same-origin /api requests.
# Example: https://heyq-api.up.railway.app  (no trailing slash, no /api suffix)
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# ─── Backend (standalone Node API, runtime) ──────────────────────────────────
# PORT is injected by most Node hosts (Railway/Render); the server honors it.
# For local runs it falls back to HEYQ_API_PORT (default 4310).
# HEYQ_API_PORT=4310

# Optional extra allowed AGENT CORS origin(s), comma-separated (e.g. a preview or
# custom HeyQ frontend domain). http://localhost:18020 and https://heyq.vercel.app
# are always allowed. Agent origins may reach every route.
# HEYQ_FRONTEND_ORIGIN=

# Optional extra allowed CUSTOMER (GGX Business+) CORS origin(s), comma-separated.
# http://localhost:18010 and https://ggx-corporate.vercel.app are always allowed.
# Customer origins may reach only the public customer surface (ticket reads +
# requester reply/reopen); agent/internal routes are refused with 403.
# HEYQ_BUSINESS_PLUS_ORIGIN=
